lzug-admin backup restore - Restore a protected backup.

Decrypt locally, validate and stage in the backend, then activate only after every precheck succeeds.

Usage:
  lzug-admin [global options] backup restore --artifact PATH [options]

Command options:
  --artifact PATH          Regular protected artifact file. Required.
  --replace                Replace a non-empty installation after creating a safety artifact. Default: false. Danger-zone confirmation.
  --identity-file PATH     Protected local age identity file.
  --identity-stdin         Read the age identity from redirected standard input. Default: false.
  --identity-prompt        Read the age identity from a hidden terminal prompt. Default: false.

Confirmation:
  Requires an interactive terminal confirmation or --force.
  --replace is a separate danger-zone confirmation and is never implied by --force.

Transport:
  Local orchestration over the shared Docker/Podman container transport; secret key material stays in the CLI.

Output:
  Human success is silent; JSON includes restore phases and safety evidence.
  --verbose adds the secret-free progress and result summary on stderr.
  --json uses the declared local result contract on stdout.

Examples:
  lzug-admin --container lzug backup restore --artifact backup.lzug --identity-file backup.agekey --force
